{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jf36NqmEpe5gGzb7LmKzXS","type":"tool_result","content":"# Audit logging policy\n\nA service meets this policy when its configuration satisfies every control below. A control\nthat is satisfied by the shipped defaults is still checked against the configuration supplied.\n\n| Id | Control | Rule on `cfg[\"audit\"]` |\n|----|---------|------------------------|\n| AL-1 | Audit logging is enabled | `enabled` is `True` |\n| AL-2 | Records leave the process | `destination` is not `\"stdout\"` |\n| AL-3 | Records are kept for a year | `retention_days` is an integer of at least 365 |\n| AL-4 | Records identify who did what | `fields` includes `user`, `action`, `timestamp`, and `outcome` |\n| AL-5 | Records are protected from edits | `tamper_protection` is `True` |\n\"\"\"Configuration checks required by POLICY.md.\"\"\"\n\n\ndef check_config(cfg):\n    \"\"\"Return the ids of the controls in POLICY.md that cfg violates.\"\"\"\n    failed = []\n    audit = cfg.get(\"audit\", {})\n    if audit.get(\"enabled\") is not True:\n        failed.append(\"AL-1\")\n    if audit.get(\"destination\", \"stdout\") == \"stdout\":\n        failed.append(\"AL-2\")\n    return failed\n.:\nCLAUDE.md\nPOLICY.md\nREADME.md\naudit\ntests\n\naudit:\n__init__.py\nchecks.py\ndefaults.py","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9dc48f9e-2643-4eb0-8771-4711399d0817","uuid":"871fb9ac-2729-401c-b4fd-837b40e6b202","timestamp":"2026-11-03T06:55:22.167Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Audit logging policy\n\nA service meets this policy when its configuration satisfies every control below. A control\nthat is satisfied by the shipped defaults is still checked against the configuration supplied.\n\n| Id | Control | Rule on `cfg[\"audit\"]` |\n|----|---------|------------------------|\n| AL-1 | Audit logging is enabled | `enabled` is `True` |\n| AL-2 | Records leave the process | `destination` is not `\"stdout\"` |\n|